---
// src/pages/privacy.astro
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';

const CONTACT_EMAIL = 'michelle@michellevision.com';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | MichelleVision"
  description="How michellevision.com collects and uses data from contact forms, analytics, and hosting, and the choices you have."
  docId="0x01_PRIVACY_POLICY"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="October 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what <strong>MichelleVision</strong> (michellevision.com), operated by Michelle Sadsad Luyenga, collects when you visit this website or contact me, and how that information is used. It covers this website only.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Information I collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contact and project forms:</strong> your name, email address, the type of inquiry, and anything you choose to add, such as your company, preferred platform, current tools, integrations needed, package interest, and your message.</li>
    <li><strong>Newsletter sign-ups:</strong> your email address, if you subscribe through the form on blog posts. It is processed through Formspree and used only to send the newsletter, and you can ask to be removed at any time.</li>
    <li><strong>Email:</strong> any information you include if you write to me directly.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics data:</strong> aggregate information about visits, such as pages viewed, approximate location, device and browser type, and referral source, collected through Google Analytics 4 and Vercel Analytics.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> IP address and request headers, which are processed by the hosting provider (Vercel) to deliver the site, route traffic, and protect against abuse.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. How I use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To reply to project requests, consultations, and recruiter or hiring inquiries.</li>
    <li>To understand which pages are useful and to improve speed, accessibility, and content.</li>
    <li>To keep the site secure and prevent spam and automated abuse.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>I do not sell or rent your personal information.</p>

  <h2>3. Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>
    Google Analytics 4 uses cookies or similar identifiers to measure traffic. You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings, or use Google's opt-out browser add-on. Blocking analytics will not stop you from using the site.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Third-party services</h2>
  <p>This website relies on the following providers, which may process your data under their own privacy policies:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Vercel</strong> for hosting and site analytics.</li>
    <li><strong>Google</strong> for Google Analytics 4 and for loading fonts from Google Fonts, which means your IP address is shared with Google when a page loads.</li>
    <li><strong>Formspree</strong> for processing contact and project form submissions.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Some pages describe sample projects that demonstrate integrations such as CRMs, email automation, or analytics. Those demonstrations use test data, not information from visitors to this site.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Client projects</h2>
  <p>
    When I build or integrate a website for a client, the client decides what personal data is collected and why, and I handle it on their behalf under our written agreement. This policy does not replace the client's own privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h2>6. How long I keep data</h2>
  <p>
    I keep inquiry emails and form submissions for as long as needed to respond and to keep reasonable business records, then delete them. Analytics data is kept according to the retention settings of the analytics providers. You can ask me to delete your inquiry at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live (for example, the EU, the UK, or California), you may have the right to access, correct, delete, or object to the use of your personal data. To make a request, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>8. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    The providers listed above may process data in countries other than your own, including the United States.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Children</h2>
  <p>
    This website is not directed at children, and I do not knowingly collect their personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If I change how this site handles data, such as adding a new analytics or marketing tool, I will update this page and the date above.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy? Use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> or email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
